@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Complex choreography — 12+ tasks, multiple participants, gateway, sub-choreography, timer.
'   usecase:      Multi-party B2B order protocol with logistics and payment participants.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Choreography - Complex Protocol

' Choreography tasks band initiator (white) / responder (grey).
' Participants: Buyer, Seller, Logistics, Bank.
' Includes: XOR gateway, event-based gateway, sub-choreography, timer event.

' --- Events ---------------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as Start
usecase " " as EndOk
usecase " " as EndFail
usecase " " as Timer ' intermediate timer event

' --- Tasks ----------------------------------------------------------------
package "Submit Order\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as T1
package "Ack Order\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T2
package "Check Stock\n[ Seller | Warehouse ]" as T3
package "Quote Shipping\n[ Seller | Logistics ]" as T4
package "Send Quote\n[ Logistics | Seller ]" as T5
package "Request Payment\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T6
package "Authorize Payment\n[ Buyer | Bank ]" as T7
package "Send Confirmation\n[ Bank | Seller ]" as T8

' Sub-choreography (collapsed) — its own banded protocol detail.
package "Fulfillment Sub-Choreography [+]\n[ Seller | Logistics ]" as SUB1

package "Confirm Shipment\n[ Logistics | Buyer ]" as T10
package "Close Order\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T11
package "Cancel Order\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T12

' --- Gateways -------------------------------------------------------------
usecase "In Stock?" as X1
usecase "Pay On Time?" as Eb1

Start --> T1
T1 --> T2
T2 --> T3
T3 --> X1
X1 --> T4 : (yes)
X1 --> T12 : (no)
T4 --> T5
T5 --> T6
T6 --> Eb1
' Event-based: first of payment or timeout
Eb1 --> T7 : Buyer pays
Eb1 --> Timer : 24h timeout
Timer --> T12
T7 --> T8
T8 --> SUB1
SUB1 --> T10
T10 --> T11
T11 --> EndOk
T12 --> EndFail

note top of SUB1
  <b>Sub-choreography (+)</b>
  Collapsed band group; its own
  participant-to-participant
  protocol (pickup, transport,
  delivery handshakes).
end note

note right of Eb1
  <b>Event-based gateway</b>
  Race: Buyer's payment vs a
  24-hour timer. First wins;
  the other is cancelled.
end note

note right of Timer
  <b>Timer intermediate event</b>
  Detects the buyer failed to
  pay within the SLA window.
end note

note bottom of T3
  <b>Multi-party choreography</b>
  Four participants, banded per
  task. Roles (initiator/responder)
  can swap between tasks.
end note

@enduml
